<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><meta charSet="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"/><link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css"><title>Colondres Owner Advisory | Independent Residential Owner’s Representative</title><meta name="description" content="Fee-only, independent construction guidance for Southern California homeowners planning major renovations, custom homes, additions, and ADUs."/><link rel="shortcut icon" href="favicon.svg"/><link rel="icon" href="favicon.svg"/>
</head><body><main><header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="#top" aria-label="Colondres Owner Advisory home"><span class="brand-mark">LC</span><span>COLONDRES <small>OWNER ADVISORY</small></span></a><nav aria-label="Primary navigation"><a href="#services">Services</a><a href="#approach">Approach</a><a href="#pricing">Fees</a><a href="#about">About</a></nav><a class="header-cta" href="#contact">Discuss your project <span>↗</span></a></header><section class="hero" id="top"><div class="hero-grid" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Independent residential owner’s representation · Southern California</p><h1>Your home.<br/><em>Your investment.</em><br/>Someone on your side.</h1><p class="hero-lede">Experienced, fee-only construction guidance for homeowners navigating major renovations, custom homes, additions, and ADUs.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button light" href="#contact">Schedule a discovery call</a><a class="text-link" href="#pledge">Read our independence pledge →</a></div></div><aside class="hero-card"><p class="card-kicker">The owner-side difference</p><blockquote>“Your contractor manages the work. We help you understand what’s happening—and represent your interests throughout the process.”</blockquote><ul><li><span>✓</span> Paid only by the homeowner</li><li><span>✓</span> No construction work</li><li><span>✓</span> No referral fees or markups</li><li><span>✓</span> Independent, documented guidance</li></ul></aside><div class="hero-foot"><span>25+ years</span><small>Construction · Project Management · Construction Management</small><b>LOS ANGELES &amp; SOUTHERN CALIFORNIA</b></div></section><section class="intro section"><p class="section-label">WHY AN OWNER’S REPRESENTATIVE</p><div><h2>A complex project shouldn’t leave the homeowner guessing.</h2><p>Designers design. Contractors build. Inspectors verify minimum code requirements. Luis provides experienced, independent support focused on the homeowner’s budget, schedule, documentation, decisions, and visible quality concerns.</p></div></section><section class="services section" id="services"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="section-label">SERVICES</p><h2>Clarity at every stage.</h2></div><p>Engage for a focused review, recurring oversight, or representation from pre-construction through closeout.</p></div><div class="service-grid"><article><span>01</span><h3>Plan &amp; select</h3><p>Scope clarity, bid leveling, contractor qualification support, and construction-focused contract observations before you commit.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Protect the budget</h3><p>Independent review of allowances, change orders, invoices, payment applications, and supporting documentation.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Track the work</h3><p>Scheduled site observations, progress photography, schedule monitoring, meeting notes, and written issue tracking.</p></article><article><span>04</span><h3>Finish with confidence</h3><p>Punch lists, closeout checklists, warranty and manual collection, and a clearer path to final completion.</p></article></div><div class="scope-strip"><span>Bid comparison</span><span>Contract observations</span><span>Change orders</span><span>Payment review</span><span>Schedules</span><span>Workmanship observations</span><span>Punch lists</span></div></section><section class="benefits section"><div class="benefits-copy"><p class="section-label">WHAT HOMEOWNERS GAIN</p><h2>Less uncertainty.<br/>Better-informed decisions.</h2><p>The goal is not to create another layer of noise. It is to bring structure, context, and accountability to the decisions that matter.</p><a class="text-link dark" href="#contact">Tell us where your project stands →</a></div><div class="benefit-list"><article><span>01</span><div><h3>Cost visibility</h3><p>Understand inclusions, exclusions, allowances, payment status, and proposed changes before approving them.</p></div></article><article><span>02</span><div><h3>Progress clarity</h3><p>Receive concise written reporting on observed progress, upcoming milestones, delays, and open decisions.</p></div></article><article><span>03</span><div><h3>Early issue awareness</h3><p>Surface visible coordination and workmanship concerns while they may be easier to address.</p></div></article><article><span>04</span><div><h3>An organized record</h3><p>Keep decisions, action items, photos, recommendations, and closeout requirements in one accountable process.</p></div></article></div></section><section class="process section" id="approach"><p class="section-label">HOW IT WORKS</p><h2>A clear, four-step engagement.</h2><div class="process-line"><article><b>01</b><h3>Discovery</h3><p>A brief call to understand your project, current stage, and primary concerns.</p></article><article><b>02</b><h3>Review</h3><p>Luis reviews available plans, proposals, agreements, budget information, and project status.</p></article><article><b>03</b><h3>Scope</h3><p>You receive a defined service plan, fee, deliverables, visit frequency, and communication rhythm.</p></article><article><b>04</b><h3>Represent</h3><p>Independent guidance and written reporting begin—focused solely on your interests.</p></article></div></section><section class="pledge" id="pledge"><div class="pledge-inner"><p class="section-label">THE INDEPENDENCE PLEDGE</p><h2>Advice without divided loyalties.</h2><p>We represent only the homeowner. We do not bid on, contract for, or self-perform construction. We accept no referral fees, commissions, rebates, markups, or other compensation from contractors, designers, subcontractors, vendors, or suppliers associated with your project.</p><div class="pledge-sign"><span>Fee-only. Owner-paid.</span><span>Affiliations disclosed.</span><span>Your interests first.</span></div></div></section><section class="pricing section" id="pricing"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="section-label">STARTING FEES</p><h2>Defined scope. Transparent fees.</h2></div><p>Final fees reflect project size, complexity, location, documents available, visit frequency, and level of involvement.</p></div><div class="price-grid"><article><p>PROJECT CLARITY SESSION</p><h3><small>Starting at</small>$500</h3><ul><li>60–90 minute consultation</li><li>Available-document review</li><li>Priority risk discussion</li><li>Written next-step summary</li></ul><a href="#contact">Request a consultation →</a></article><article class="featured"><span class="tag">MOST COMMON START</span><p>BID &amp; SCOPE REVIEW</p><h3><small>Starting at</small>$1,500</h3><ul><li>Up to three bid comparisons</li><li>Scope gaps and allowance review</li><li>Clarification question log</li><li>Decision briefing</li></ul><a href="#contact">Discuss your bids →</a></article><article><p>ONGOING REPRESENTATION</p><h3><small>Starting at</small>$3,000<em>/mo</em></h3><ul><li>Scheduled site observations</li><li>Progress and issue reporting</li><li>Change and payment review</li><li>Schedule and closeout tracking</li></ul><a href="#contact">Request a custom scope →</a></article></div><p class="pricing-note">Focused site observations with written reports may also be scoped individually, typically from $650 per visit. Fees shown are launch guidance and should be confirmed before publication.</p></section><section class="about section" id="about"><div class="about-card"><div class="monogram">LC</div><p>INDEPENDENT<br/>OWNER-SIDE<br/>GUIDANCE</p></div><div class="about-copy"><p class="section-label">ABOUT LUIS</p><h2>Construction experience, translated for homeowners.</h2><p>Luis Colondres brings more than 25 years of construction, project-management, and construction-management experience, including contractor-side and owner-side work and extensive public-works exposure.</p><p>His background includes working with plans and specifications, schedules, RFIs, submittals, change orders, payment applications, project controls, and closeout documentation. This service brings that disciplined perspective to residential owners—without performing the construction and without financial ties to the project team.</p><div class="about-stats"><span><b>25+</b>Years of experience</span><span><b>2</b>Owner &amp; contractor perspectives</span><span><b>1</b>Client: the homeowner</span></div></div></section><section class="faq section"><p class="section-label">FREQUENTLY ASKED</p><h2>Straight answers before we begin.</h2><div class="faq-list"><details open=""><summary>Are you a contractor?<span>+</span></summary><p>No. This service does not bid, contract for, or perform construction. Luis works as the homeowner’s independent advisor and representative.</p></details><details><summary>Do you replace my architect or contractor?<span>+</span></summary><p>No. The architect leads design and the contractor leads construction. The owner’s representative helps the homeowner understand, coordinate, document, and evaluate the project from the owner’s side.</p></details><details><summary>Do you inspect or certify the work?<span>+</span></summary><p>Site visits are observational and do not replace required inspections, testing, engineering, architectural services, or code enforcement. Visible concerns are documented for follow-up by the appropriate project professional.</p></details><details><summary>Is contract review legal advice?<span>+</span></summary><p>No. Contract observations are provided from a construction-management perspective. Homeowners should use a qualified attorney for legal review and advice.</p></details><details><summary>When should I bring you in?<span>+</span></summary><p>Ideally before selecting a contractor or signing a construction contract. Support can also begin during construction when a homeowner needs clarity, documentation, or independent guidance.</p></details><details><summary>What projects are the best fit?<span>+</span></summary><p>Major renovations, additions, custom homes, ADUs, hillside projects, and other complex residential work where the decisions and financial exposure justify professional owner-side support.</p></details></div></section><section class="contact section" id="contact"><div class="contact-copy"><p class="section-label">START A CONVERSATION</p><h2>Bring clarity to your next construction decision.</h2><p>Share a few details about your project. A 15–20 minute discovery call can help determine whether independent owner-side support is the right fit.</p><div class="placeholder-contact"><strong>REPLACE BEFORE LAUNCH</strong><span>Phone: (XXX) XXX-XXXX</span><span>Email: hello@yourdomain.com</span><span>Website: www.yourdomain.com</span><span>Service area: Southern California</span></div></div><form aria-label="Project inquiry form"><label>NAME<input required="" autoComplete="name" placeholder="Your name" name="name"/></label><label>EMAIL<input required="" type="email" autoComplete="email" placeholder="you@example.com" name="email"/></label><div class="form-row"><label>PHONE<input autoComplete="tel" placeholder="(XXX) XXX-XXXX" name="phone"/></label><label>PROJECT LOCATION<input placeholder="City or neighborhood" name="location"/></label></div><label>PROJECT TYPE<select name="projectType"><option value="" disabled="" selected="">Select one</option><option>Major renovation</option><option>Custom home</option><option>Addition or ADU</option><option>Construction already underway</option><option>Other residential project</option></select></label><label>HOW CAN WE HELP?<textarea required="" name="message" placeholder="Tell us the project stage, estimated budget, and your biggest concern." rows="5"></textarea></label><button type="submit">Send project inquiry <span>↗</span></button><small>PLACEHOLDER FORM — connect to Formspree, Netlify Forms, your CRM, or a secure email handler before publishing.</small></form></section><footer><a class="brand footer-brand" href="#top"><span class="brand-mark">LC</span><span>COLONDRES <small>OWNER ADVISORY</small></span></a><p>Independent homeowner construction advocacy 